IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `gst-types`
IMPORT `gst-charge`
IMPORT `gst-registration`
IMPORT `gst-credit`
IMPORT `gst-administration`
IMPORT `gst-penalties`

-- Goods and Services Tax Act 1993 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this supply: is GST charged on it, and how — standard-rated,
--    zero-rated, exempt or outside the scope; when does it take place; at
--    what rate; how much tax is in the price; and who accounts for it?"
--
-- One answer through Goal 1. Registration (Goal 2), input tax (Goal 3),
-- assessment and appeal (Goal 4), collection and rulings (Goal 5) and
-- penalties (Goal 6) answer their own questions in their modules.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `GST position` HAS
    `treatment`                                      IS A `Tax treatment`
    `made in Singapore`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `time of supply`                                 IS A MAYBE DATE
    `rate per cent`                                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `tax on the supply`                              IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the recipient accounts under the reverse charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the customer accounts under s 38 or 38A`        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 8, 11, 13, 14(2), 16, 17(2), (2A), (3A), 21, 22, 38, 38A; Third Schedule
GIVEN c IS A `Supply case`
GIVETH A `GST position`
`the GST position for` c MEANS
    `GST position` WITH
        `treatment`                                      IS
            IF (`the case is reverse charged` c) THEN `standard-rated` ELSE `the tax treatment of` (c's `supply`)
        `made in Singapore`                              IS `the supply is made in Singapore` (c's `supply`)
        `time of supply`                                 IS `the time of supply of` (c's `supply`)
        `rate per cent`                                  IS
            CONSIDER `the time of supply of` (c's `supply`)
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the rate of tax per cent on` t)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `tax on the supply`                              IS
            CONSIDER `the time of supply of` (c's `supply`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN
                IF (`the case is reverse charged` c)
                THEN JUST (c's `supply`'s `consideration in money` TIMES (`the rate of tax per cent on` t) DIVIDED BY 100)
                ELSE IF `the tax treatment of` (c's `supply`) EQUALS `standard-rated`
                     THEN JUST (`the value after the special rule` (c's `special value`) `, value` (`the value of a supply for` (c's `supply`'s `consideration in money`) `at` (`the rate of tax per cent on` t) `per cent`) TIMES (`the rate of tax per cent on` t) DIVIDED BY 100)
                     ELSE JUST 0
        `the recipient accounts under the reverse charge` IS
            CONSIDER c's `reverse charge`
            WHEN JUST r  THEN `the recipient accounts for tax under the reverse charge` r
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        `the customer accounts under s 38 or 38A`        IS c's `supply`'s `customer accounts for the tax (s 38, 38A)`

-- s 14(2): the recipient is treated as making a taxable supply in Singapore;
-- s 17(3A), (2A)(a): its value is the whole consideration, and the tax is
-- added to it, not taken out of it.
@ref s 14(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Supply case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case is reverse charged` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `reverse charge`
    WHEN JUST r  THEN `the recipient accounts for tax under the reverse charge` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
